🐛 Fix TypeAliasType list query params only keeping the last value

I started by comparing Cookie, Header, and Query to see if they behave the same for aliases, defaults, and lists.

A plain list query param worked:

```python
@app.get("/q")
def q(v: Annotated[list[str], Query()]):
    return {"v": v}

# GET /q?v=a&v=b&v=c  →  {"v": ["a", "b", "c"]}
```

Then I wrapped that same list in a `TypeAliasType` (the same shape as a PEP 695 `type Tags = list[str]` alias):

```python
Tags = TypeAliasType("Tags", list[str])

@app.get("/q")
def q(v: Annotated[Tags, Query()]):
    return {"v": v}
```

The same request came back as **422**. FastAPI treated the alias as a scalar and only kept the last value (`"c"`).

I traced it to `field_annotation_is_sequence()`. `_get_multidict_value()` uses that helper to choose between `.getlist()` and `.get()`. It already unwraps `Annotated` and unions, but not `TypeAliasType`, so the alias never looked like a sequence.

This PR unwraps the alias before that check, and adds a Query regression test so repeated values come through as a list again.

Related discussion: https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/16222

The same helper is also used for Form models (https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/16100, https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/pull/16111). Happy to coordinate if maintainers prefer one combined change.
